  "hypothesis": "The previous FINRA days-to-cover haircut failed, suggesting the high-crowding state may contain squeeze convexity rather than only risk. The squeeze thesis should stay narrow: only already-qualified trend/breakout stocks with same-day top-quartile days-to-cover and production-visible RS20 plus own-green demand confirmation receive a small cap-aware allocation top-up.",
  "interpretation": "FINRA high days-to-cover plus RS20/own-green demand confirmation did not clear the canonical three-window gate as a short-squeeze top-up.",
  "known_risks": [
    "FINRA is biweekly and delayed; it is PIT-safe but stale relative to daily price action.",
